% =============================================================================
% grill — graded μMALL: gill + least/greatest fixed points (μ/ν)
% =============================================================================
%
% The first calculus combining BOTH unification axes in one place:
%   - GRADES (gill): a grade algebra as DATA — the graded exponential !_g A,
%     the graded lax monad {B}@d, the graded transport comonad !!_d A (haul),
%     scheduled by whichever semiring the config plugs in.
%   - FIXPOINTS (fill/μMALL): least/greatest fixed points μ/ν, cyclic proofs,
%     coinduction.
%
% This is the concrete "graded μMALL" experiment (the grade×fixpoint bridge,
% THY_0044-to-be): does the resource-semiring grade compose soundly with μ/ν?
% The surface is INHERITED, not copied: @extends gill (loadChain merges gill's
% whole graded surface — ILL's connectives + till's graded monad/bang + gill's
% dist/haul/weight), and grill declares ONLY the fixpoint connectives below.
% @category fixpoint arms deriveRoles' lfp/gfp exactly as in fill, so the
% generic cyclic-proof engine (bridge/gtc-check/focused) activates over the
% graded surface with no engine change — the grades ride the same rules.

@family grill.
@extends gill.

% Least fixed point μX.B(X) — inductive data (verbatim from fill; @category
% fixpoint → roles.lfp). Positive: μL invertible / eager, μR needs focus.
mu: formula -> formula
  @ascii "mu _"
  @latex "\\mu #1"
  @prec 45 right
  @category fixpoint
  @polarity positive.

% Greatest fixed point νX.B(X) — coinductive data / signals (→ roles.gfp).
% Negative: νR invertible / eager, νL needs focus.
nu: formula -> formula
  @ascii "nu _"
  @latex "\\nu #1"
  @prec 45 right
  @category fixpoint
  @polarity negative.
